A||||4||V8Fiero||Need help with charging system.||||8||
Z||000000||V8Fiero||07-23-2001||07:44 PM||||Ok, <P>Heres whats happening so far. New alternator in my V6. (it was for a 4cyl but that shouldnt matter, should it?) Brand new battery. I start the car up and the volt guage is right at 13,14 or so. No volt light either. But after awhile the voltage drops down around 10 or so and the volt light comes on. Once in awhile the voltage goes back up, and then drops again. Only twice has it totally drained the battery and left me needing a boost. Just put a brand new battery in at the store. Drove home without a hitch. Let the car run for a few in the driveway, and it started to do the same thing. Must be in the wiring somewhere, but where do I start? I know the connections are good at the alternator. Already have taken it out once and took it in to have it checked. Please help. Im baffled.<P>Scott<P>------------------<BR>86 SE Gold<BR>86 GT Red <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/RedRavensig.JPG"> <BR>"Trying to change from V8Fiero to RedRavenGT"||||reg||8
Z||000001||PBJ||07-23-2001||08:02 PM||||Sounds like an alternator problem-that is related to heat.  As you said you had your alt checked out but was it hot (in the car acting up) or at the store?  Within the alt you have a voltage regulator, diodes, brushes, stator-all sorts of components that can and are affected by heat-I would suggest you rebuild the alternator, it is not a hard job and is cheaper than buying a rebuilt one.<P>If you are certain all conections are good than you are left with the alt.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||07-23-2001||08:27 PM||||Take it someplace that has a tester that can be wheeled/carried out to the car and test in situ with everything hot.<P>Check all the terminals below the big black box connector next to the battery.||||reg||1
Z||000003||V8Fiero||07-23-2001||09:23 PM||||I was wondering about the heat issue on the alternator. I did have to splice some wires on the fuse box? next to the battery when I changed the engine. I will check them also.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||V8Fiero||07-23-2001||09:59 PM||||As I stated above the alternator is brand new. Only had it for 2 months. I checked my splices and they were good. I started it up again after it cooled down and it started out with low voltage. Ran for about 10 mins and then jumped back up to good voltage for about 5 mins. then back down she went. Im gonna take the car to the shop tomorrow and have them check the alt in the car.<P><P>------------------<BR>86 SE Gold<BR>86 GT Red <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/RedRavensig.JPG"> <BR>"Trying to change from V8Fiero to RedRavenGT"||||reg||1
